# AWS — RDS + DB Tunnels (Example)

Created: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC

## Preferred Safety Defaults
- Use read-only DB users for production.
- Enforce timeouts and row limits.
- Avoid direct connections from laptops unless the org explicitly allows it.

## Common Connection Patterns
- VPN + security group allowlist
- Bastion host (SSH tunnel)
- SSM port-forwarding

Example SSH tunnel:
```sh
ssh -N -L 5432:<rds-endpoint>:5432 ec2-user@<bastion-host>
psql "postgres://readonly@localhost:5432/app"
```

## Operational Gotchas
- If queries are slow, stop and add predicates/limits instead of “waiting it out”.
- If you need `EXPLAIN`, confirm it’s allowed in prod and capture results as evidence.

